definition 7.
plane is a surface for which the following holds:
    let
        P be an instance of plane and
        A be an instance of point and
        B be an instance of point and
        AB be an instance of finite straight line and
        T be an instance of point
    if
        A lies anywhere on P and
        B lies anywhere on P and
        A is not equal to B and
        AB is bounded by A, B and
        T lies on AB
    then 
        T lies on P.
what is a plane.

