definition 8.
angle is defined by the following rule: 
    let
        A be an instance of point and
        S be an instance of point and
        B be an instance of point and
        AS be an instance of finite line and
        SB be an instance of finite line
    only if
        AS is bounded by A, S and
        SB is bounded by S, B and
        A not on SB and
        B not on AS
    then
        the construct which includes AS, SB defines an angle.

