    does X equal Y?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Rule 'condition of being lies on' failed to deduce equality from mutual incidence.`
end Logos State on rule condition of being lies on 2.

    common rule condition of point being in between other two points.
        let
            A be an instance of point and
            B be an instance of point and
            C be an instance of point and
            AB be an instance of finite straight line and
            AC be an instance of finite straight line and
            BC be an instance of finite straight line
        if
            AB is bounded by A,B and
            AC is bounded by A,C and
            BC is bounded by B,C and
            AC is truncation of AB
        then
            C lies between A and B and
            BC is truncation of AB and
            AB is extension of BC and
            AB is extension of AC.

          

start Logos State on rule condition of point being in between other two points 1.
    P1 is an instance of point.
    P2 is an instance of point.
    P3 is an instance of point.
    L12 is an instance of finite straight line.
    L12 is bounded by P1 and P2.
    L13 is an instance of finite straight line.
    L13 is bounded by P1 and P3.
    L23 is an instance of finite straight line.
    L23 is bounded by P2 and P3.

    L13 is truncation of L12.
  
    is P3 lies between P1 and P2?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Deduction failed: Point P3 should lie between P1 and P2.`

    is L23 truncation of L12?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Deduction failed: L23 should be recognized as a truncation of L12.`

    is L12 extension of L23?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Deduction failed: L12 should be recognized as an extension of L23.`

    is L12 extension of L13?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Deduction failed: L12 should be recognized as an extension of L13.`
end Logos State on rule condition of point being in between other two points 1.
            
    common rule condition of point being in between via extension.
        let
            A be an instance of point and
            B be an instance of point and
            C be an instance of point and
            AB be an instance of finite straight line and
        if    
            AB is bounded by A,B and
            AC be an instance of finite straight line and
            AC is bounded by A,C and
            BC be an instance of finite straight line and
            BC is bounded by B,C and
            AC is extension of AB
        then
            B lies between A and C.


start Logos State on rule condition of point being in between via extension 1.
    P1 is an instance of point.
    P2 is an instance of point.
    P3 is an instance of point.
    L12 is an instance of finite straight line.
    L12 is bounded by P1 and P2.
    L13 is an instance of finite straight line.
    L13 is bounded by P1 and P3.

    ~ This triggers the rule 'condition of point being in between via extension' ~
    L13 is extension of L12.

    is P2 lies between P1 and P3?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Deduction failed: Point P2 should lie between P1 and P3 via extension logic.`
end Logos State on rule condition of point being in between via extension 1.
                   

    common rule condition of kinematic persistence.
        let 
            L be an instance of finite straight line and
            L_ext be an instance of finite straight line
        if 
            L_ext is extension of L
        then 
            L is a part of L_ext and
            L_ext contains L.

start Logos State on rule condition of kinematic persistence 1.
    L1 is an instance of finite straight line.
    L2 is an instance of finite straight line.
    L2 is extension of L1.
    
    is L1 a part of L2?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Rule 'condition of kinematic persistence' failed to deduce part-of relationship.`

    does L2 contain L1?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Rule 'condition of kinematic persistence' failed to deduce containment.`
end Logos State on rule condition of kinematic persistence 1.

    common rule condition of extrusion magnitude.
        ~ Newton's Fluxion: Magnitude is generated by movement ~
        let
            A be an instance of anything and
            B be an instance of anything
        if
            A is extrusion from B
        then
           A is greater than B and
            B is an intrusion of A. 



start Logos State on extrusion magnitude 1.
    P1 is an instance of point.
    L1 is an instance of finite straight line.
    
    ~ Line L1 is generated by the movement of point P1 ~
    L1 is extrusion from P1.

    is L1 greater than P1?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Rule 'condition of extrusion magnitude' failed to deduce magnitude increase.`
    is P1 an intrusion of L1?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Rule 'condition of extrusion magnitude' failed to deduce inverse intrusion relationship.`
end Logos State on extrusion magnitude 1.

start Logos State 1.
    AB is an instance of line.
    AC is an instance of line.
    BC is an instance of line.
    AB is equal to AC.
    AC is equal to BC.
    does AB equal BC?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Transitivity test failed in Logos State 1.`
end Logos State 1.

start Logos State on Magnitude Transitivity.
    A is an instance of anything.
    B is an instance of anything.
    C is an instance of anything.
    A is greater than B.
    B is greater than C.
    is A greater than C?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Magnitude transitivity (A > B > C) failed.`
end Logos State on Magnitude Transitivity.

start Logos State on Magnitude Substitution.
    A is an instance of anything.
    B is an instance of anything.
    C is an instance of anything.
    A is less than B.
    B is equal to C.
    is A less than C?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Magnitude substitution (A < B, B = C) failed.`
end Logos State on Magnitude Substitution.

start Logos State on Postulate 4 Right Angle Equality.
    RR1 is an instance of right angle.
    RR2 is an instance of right angle.
    does RR1 equal RR2?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Postulate 4 application failed: All right angles should be equal.`
end Logos State on Postulate 4 Right Angle Equality.

start Logos State on Postulate 5 Whole and Part.
    Whole is an instance of anything.
    Part is an instance of anything.
    Part is a part of Whole.
    is Whole greater than Part?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Postulate 5 application failed: The whole must be greater than its part.`
end Logos State on Postulate 5 Whole and Part.

start Logos State on Nested Part-of logic.
    X is an instance of anything.
    Y is an instance of anything.
    X lies on Y.
    X is not equal to Y.
    is X part of Y?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Deduction of part-of from incidence and non-equality failed.`
end Logos State on Nested Part-of logic.

~------------ Advanced Geometric Rules ------------~
    common rule incidence transitivity.
        let
            A be an instance of anything and
            B be an instance of anything and
            C be an instance of anything
        if
            A lies on B and
            B lies on C
        then
            A lies on C.
    common rule equality symmetry.
        let
            A be an instance of anything and
            B be an instance of anything
        if
            A is equal to B
        then
            B is equal to A.

    common rule circle intersection.
        let
            C1 be an instance of circle and
            C2 be an instance of circle and
            P be an instance of point and
            CF1 be an instance of circumference and
            CF2 be an instance of circumference
        if
            CF1 is a circumference of C1 and
            CF2 is a circumference of C2 and
            P lies on CF1 and
            P lies on CF2
        then
            P is at intersection of C1 and C2.

    common rule part whole transitivity.
        let
            A be an instance of anything and
            B be an instance of anything and
            C be an instance of anything
        if
            A is a part of B and
            B is a part of C
        then
            A is a part of C.

    common rule point on segment.
        let
            A be an instance of point and
            B be an instance of point and
            C be an instance of point and
            AB be an instance of finite straight line
        if
            AB is bounded by A and B and
            C lies between A and B
        then
            C lies on AB.

    common rule equilateral triangle actualization.
        let
            T be an instance of triangle and
            Side1 be an instance of finite straight line and
            Side2 be an instance of finite straight line and
            Side3 be an instance of finite straight line
        if
            T is bounded by Side1 and
            T is bounded by Side2 and
            T is bounded by Side3 and
            Side1 is equal to Side2 and
            Side2 is equal to Side3 and
            Side3 is equal to Side1
        then
            T is an instance of equilateral triangle.

start Logos State equilateral triangle actualization rule test.

    T is an instance of triangle.
    Side1 is an instance of finite straight line.
    Side2 is an instance of finite straight line.
    Side3 is an instance of finite straight line.

    T is bounded by Side1.
    T is bounded by Side2.
    T is bounded by Side3.
    Side1 is equal to Side2.
    Side2 is equal to Side3.
    Side3 is equal to Side1.

    is T an instance of equilateral triangle?

    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `equilateral triangle actualization rule test failed.`
end Logos State equilateral triangle actualization rule test.


start Logos State on Incidence Transitivity.
    P1 is an instance of point.
    L1 is an instance of line.
    Plane1 is an instance of plane.
    P1 lies on L1.
    L1 lies on Plane1.
    is P1 lies on Plane1?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Incidence transitivity (Point -> Line -> Plane) failed.`
end Logos State on Incidence Transitivity.

start Logos State on Circle Property Actualization.
    C1 is an instance of circle.
    C is an instance of point.
    A is an instance of point.
    B is an instance of point.
    CF1 is an instance of circumference.
    CA is an instance of finite straight line.
    CB is an instance of finite straight line.
    
    CF1 is a circumference of C1.
    C is a center of C1.
    A lies on CF1.
    B lies on CF1.
    CA is bounded by C and A.
    CB is bounded by C and B.
    A is not equal to B.

    ~ Definition 16 rule: then the CA length is equal to CB length ~
    does CA equal CB?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Circle radii equality deduction failed.`
end Logos State on Circle Property Actualization.

start Logos State on Proposition 1 Core Logic.
    A is an instance of point.
    B is an instance of point.
    C is an instance of point.
    AB is an instance of finite straight line.
    AC is an instance of finite straight line.
    BC is an instance of finite straight line.
    C1 is an instance of circle.
    C2 is an instance of circle.
    CF1 is an instance of circumference.
    CF2 is an instance of circumference.

    CF1 is a circumference of C1.
    A is a center of C1.
    B lies on CF1.
    C lies on CF1.
    AB is bounded by A and B.
    AC is bounded by A and C.
    A is not equal to B.
    A is not equal to C.

    CF2 is a circumference of C2.
    B is a center of C2.
    A lies on CF2.
    C lies on CF2.
    BC is bounded by B and C.
    A is not equal to B.
    B is not equal to C.
    A is not equal to C.
    ~ BA is symmetric to AB ~
    
    ~ Goal: Prove AC = BC because AC=AB and BC=AB ~
    is AC equal to BC?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Proposition 1 logical chain (AC=AB, BC=AB => AC=BC) failed.`
end Logos State on Proposition 1 Core Logic.

start Logos State on Equilateral Triangle Actualization.
    T1 is an instance of triangle.
    S1 is an instance of finite straight line.
    S2 is an instance of finite straight line.
    S3 is an instance of finite straight line.
    T1 is bounded by S1, S2, S3.
    
    S1 is equal to S2.
    S2 is equal to S3.
    S3 is equal to S1.

    is T1 an equilateral triangle?
    assert last answer: `Yes.`
    error message: `Equilateral triangle actualization failed.`
end Logos State on Equilateral Triangle Actualization.

