    common rule perpendicularity symmetry.
        let
            L1 be an instance of finite straight line and
            L2 be an instance of finite straight line
        if
            L1 is perpendicular to L2
        then
            L2 is perpendicular to L1.

    common rule equality substitution in incidence.
        let
            A be an instance of anything and
            B be an instance of anything and
            C be an instance of anything
        if
            A lies on B and
            B is equal to C
        then
            A lies on C.

    common rule diameter center relationship.
        let
            D be an instance of diameter and
            C1 be an instance of circle and
            P be an instance of point
        if
            D is a diameter of C1 and
            P is a center of C1
        then
            P lies on D and
            D contains P.

