start Way of Logos  Book1 proposition 1.
    given Logos State
        A is an instance of a point.
        A position is known.
        B is an instance of a point.
        B position is known.
        AB is an instance of finite straight line.
        AB is bounded by A,B.
    target Logos State includes given Logos State plus:
        C is an instance of a point.
        AC is an instance of finite straight line.
        BC is an instance of finite straight line.
        BC is bounded by B,C.
        AC is bounded by A,C.
        ABC is an instance of equilateral triangle.
        ABC is bounded by AB,AC,BC.

    start Logos Path.
        draw circle C1 with center B and passing through A according to Postulate 3 where B is C and A is R.
        draw circle C2 with center A and passing through B according to Postulate 3 where A is C and B is R.
        draw point C which lies at intersection of C1 and C2.
        draw line BC according to postulate Book1 postulate 1 where B is A and C is B.
        draw line AC according to postulate Book1 postulate 1 where A is A and C is B.
        AC is equal to AB due to the definition 15.
        BC is equal to AB due to the  Book1 definition.
        AC is equal to BC following Book1 common notion.
        draw instance of equilateral triangle ABC bounded by AB,BC,AC.
    end Logos Path.

    acknowledgement: the definition 15 defines
            ABC as an instance of equilateral triangle bounded by AB,BC,AC. 
        
    assert ABC is an instance of equilateral triangle.
end Way of Logos Book1 proposition 1.




