start Way of Logos of Book1 proposition 2.
    given Logos State
        A is an instance of a point.
        A position is known.
        B is an instance of a point.
        B position is known.
        C is an instance of a point.
        C position is known.
        BC is an instance of finite straight line.
        BC is bounded by B,C.
        
    target Logos State includes given Logos State plus:
        L is an instance of a point.
        L position is unknown.
        AL is an instance of finite straight line.
        AL is bounded by A,L.
        AL is equal to BC.

    start Logos Path.
        draw line AB according to Book of Euclid postulate 1 where A is A and B is B.
        draw instance of equilateral triangle DAB bounded by AB,BD,DA 
            according to Way of Logos  Book1 proposition 1 where A is A and B is B and AB is AB.
        draw line BF as an extension of DB following Book of Euclid postulate 2 where D is C and B is D and DB is CD.
        draw circle C1 with center B and passing through C according to Book of Euclid postulate 3 where B is C and C is R.
        draw point G which lies at intersection of C1 and BF.
        draw line AE as an extension of DA following Book of Euclid postulate 2 where D is C and A is D and DA is CD.
        draw circle C2 with center D and passing through G according to Book of Euclid postulate 3 where D is C and G is R.
        draw point L which lies at intersection of C2 and AE.
        draw line AL according to Book of Euclid postulate 1 where A is A and L is B.
        
        BG is equal to BC due to the definition 15.
        DL is equal to DG due to the definition 15.
        DA is equal to DB following Book1 proposition 1.
        AL is equal to BG following Book1 common notion 3.
        AL is equal to BC following Book1 common notion 1.
    end Logos Path.

    acknowledgement: AL is equal to BC.

    assert AL is equal to BC.
end Way of Logos of Book1 proposition 2.

